# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the WEK test suites.
#
# Referenced by tools/scripts/preflight.sh's --tsan leg:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/tools/scripts/tsan.supp ..." ./build/.../scenescript_tests
#
# Scope: suppress KNOWN-BENIGN reports from third-party runtime internals only
# (Qt/glib lazy static init, libstdc++'s atomic<shared_ptr> sharded-lock impl,
# the dynamic loader).  Keep entries NARROW (library-prefix / well-known
# function), never silence first-party (wallpaper::*) frames — those are the
# races the leg exists to catch.
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions
# `race:<substr>` matches the function name OR the library; `called_from_lib:`
# matches when the racy access originates inside the named shared library.

# ── Qt internals ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# QMetaType / QObject / QJSEngine one-time lazy init touched from the Qt event
# machinery (scenescript_tests instantiates QJSEngine + SceneTimerBridge).
called_from_lib:libQt6Core
called_from_lib:libQt6Qml
called_from_lib:libQt6Gui
race:QMetaType
race:QtPrivate::

# ── glib (pulled in transitively by Qt platform/dbus) ────────────────────────
called_from_lib:libglib-2.0
called_from_lib:libgobject-2.0
race:g_private_get
race:g_slice

# ── libstdc++ runtime ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# std::atomic<std::shared_ptr<T>> is implemented with a sharded spinlock/mutex
# table in libstdc++; its internal bookkeeping can surface as benign reports.
# Also covers libstdc++'s own lazy locale/facet init.
called_from_lib:libstdc++
race:__gnu_cxx::

# ── dynamic loader / C runtime ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dlopen of Qt plugins and __cxa_* one-time guards.
called_from_lib:libc.so
race:__cxa_
